# Unit18
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit18核心词汇

vary/ˈveri/变化/Prices vary from store to store.
vast/væst/广阔的/The vast desert stretches for miles.
vehicle/ˈviːɪkl/车辆/Cars are the most common vehicle in the city.
venture/ˈventʃər/风险投资/He started a new venture in the tech industry.
verify/ˈverɪfaɪ/验证/Please verify the information before publishing.
version/ˈvɜːrʒn/版本/This is the latest version of the software.
victim/ˈvɪktɪm/受害者/The victims of the earthquake received aid.
violate/ˈvaɪəleɪt/违反/He violated the terms of the contract.
violence/ˈvaɪələns/暴力/The government condemned the violence.
virtual/ˈvɜːrtʃuəl/虚拟的/She attended a virtual meeting from home.
visible/ˈvɪzəbl/看得见的/The mountain is visible from the city.
vital/ˈvaɪtl/至关重要的/Water is vital for human survival.
vivid/ˈvɪvɪd/生动的/She gave a vivid description of the scene.
volume/ˈvɑːljuːm/音量；体积/Turn down the volume, please.
voluntary/ˈvɑːlənteri/自愿的/Participation in the program is voluntary.
vote/voʊt/投票/Every citizen has the right to vote.
vulnerable/ˈvʌlnərəbl/脆弱的/Children are particularly vulnerable to disease.
wage/weɪdʒ/工资/He earns a decent wage.
wander/ˈwɑːndər/漫步/She wandered through the streets of Paris.
warn/wɔːrn/警告/The sign warns people of the danger.
waste/weɪst/浪费/Don't waste your time on trivial matters.
wealth/welθ/财富/Health is more important than wealth.
weapon/ˈwepən/武器/The country developed new weapons.
weird/wɪrd/奇怪的/There is a weird smell in this room.
welfare/ˈwelfer/福利/The government increased welfare spending.
widespread/ˈwaɪdspred/广泛的/There is widespread support for the policy.
withdraw/wɪðˈdrɔː/撤退；取款/He withdrew money from the bank.
witness/ˈwɪtnəs/目击者/The witness testified in court.
worthwhile/ˌwɜːrθˈwaɪl/值得的/It is a worthwhile investment.
yield/jiːld/产出；让步/The farm yields a good harvest every year.
absorb/əbˈzɔːrb/吸收/Plants absorb sunlight for energy.
accommodate/əˈkɑːmədeɪt/适应/We must accommodate different viewpoints.
acknowledge/əkˈnɑːlɪdʒ/承认/He acknowledged his mistake publicly.
acquisition/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃn/收购/The company announced a major acquisition.
adequate/ˈædɪkwət/足够的/The supply is adequate for our needs.
advocate/ˈædvəkeɪt/提倡/She advocates for equal rights.
aggregate/ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt/总计/The aggregate score was 3-1.
allocate/ˈæləkeɪt/分配/The government allocated funds for research.
ambiguous/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/模糊的/The contract contains ambiguous language.
anticipate/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/预料/We anticipate a rise in demand.
apparatus/ˌæpəˈrætəs/装置/The laboratory has modern apparatus.
appendix/əˈpendɪks/附录/See the appendix for more details.
appliance/əˈplaɪəns/家用电器/The store sells household appliances.
appraisal/əˈpreɪzl/评估/We conducted a thorough appraisal of the property.
apprehend/ˌæprɪˈhend/逮捕/The police apprehended the suspect.
arbitrary/ˈɑːrbrɪteri/任意的/The decision seemed arbitrary and unfair.
array/əˈreɪi/一系列/There is an array of options to choose from.
articulate/ɑːrˈtɪkjuleɪt/清晰表达/She articulated her ideas clearly.
aspire/əˈspaɪər/渴望/She aspires to become a doctor.
assault/əˈsɔːlt/袭击/He was charged with assault.
